[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3460126030","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/112114#issuecomment-3460126030","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112114","id":3460126030,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7OPVVO","user":{"login":"bruvzg","id":7645683,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc2NDU2ODM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7645683?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg","html_url":"https://github.com/bruvzg","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-29T07:08:23Z","updated_at":"2025-10-29T07:08:23Z","body":"The issue seems to be `is_open`, which stay `true` after pipe is dead. `get_length()` works as expected.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3460126030/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3460330741","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/112114#issuecomment-3460330741","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112114","id":3460330741,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7OQHT1","user":{"login":"bruvzg","id":7645683,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc2NDU2ODM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7645683?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg","html_url":"https://github.com/bruvzg","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-29T08:23:32Z","updated_at":"2025-10-29T08:23:32Z","body":"Note: while unnecessary error spam is Windows specific, `is_open` is behaving the same, so this code will hang indefinitely on any platform, since it's checking only if our end of the pipe is open, and do it for both stdin and stdout and return true if either is open.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3460330741/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3460336944","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/112114#issuecomment-3460336944","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112114","id":3460336944,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7OQI0w","user":{"login":"bruvzg","id":7645683,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc2NDU2ODM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7645683?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg","html_url":"https://github.com/bruvzg","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-29T08:25:28Z","updated_at":"2025-10-29T08:45:52Z","body":"As a workaround for 4.5, you can use `OS.is_process_running(pipe[\"pid\"])` to determine when it's done (and read the remaining data for the pipe after).\n\n\n```gdscript\n\twhile stdio.is_open():\n\t\tvar sz = pipe[\"stdio\"].get_length()\n\t\tif sz > 0:\n\t\t\tvar buffer = pipe[\"stdio\"].get_buffer(sz) as PackedByteArray\n\t\t\t$TextEdit.text += buffer.get_string_from_multibyte_char()\n\t\telse:\n\t\t\tif stdio.get_error() == Error.ERR_FILE_CANT_READ:\n\t\t\t\tbreak\n\t\t\tif !OS.is_process_running(pipe[\"pid\"]):\n\t\t\t\tbreak\n```","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3460336944/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3466604004","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/112114#issuecomment-3466604004","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112114","id":3466604004,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7OoC3k","user":{"login":"CsloudX","id":35988767,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1OTg4NzY3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/35988767?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/CsloudX","html_url":"https://github.com/CsloudX","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CsloudX/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CsloudX/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CsloudX/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CsloudX/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CsloudX/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CsloudX/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CsloudX/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CsloudX/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CsloudX/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-30T08:18:01Z","updated_at":"2025-10-30T08:18:01Z","body":"> As a workaround for 4.5, you can use `OS.is_process_running(pipe[\"pid\"])` to determine when it's done (and read the remaining data for the pipe after).\n> \n> \twhile stdio.is_open():\n> \t\tvar sz = pipe[\"stdio\"].get_length()\n> \t\tif sz > 0:\n> \t\t\tvar buffer = pipe[\"stdio\"].get_buffer(sz) as PackedByteArray\n> \t\t\t$TextEdit.text += buffer.get_string_from_multibyte_char()\n> \t\telse:\n> \t\t\tif stdio.get_error() == Error.ERR_FILE_CANT_READ:\n> \t\t\t\tbreak\n> \t\t\tif !OS.is_process_running(pipe[\"pid\"]):\n> \t\t\t\tbreak\n\nOh, I'm tested this. it not work sometimes. when OS.is_process_running(pipe[\"pid\"]) return false, but pipe[\"stdio\"].get_buffer(sz) like have some data not read. i'm test `ping 127.0.0.1`","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3466604004/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":1},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]